# TR1-control-timed: TIMED arm A of the paired timing ABAB on coding prompts (audits OFF) for lever V6 (the ring fabric). Arms alternate A B A B in this one image, each
# after its own all-four reset, same admission order: A = c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace (the control, production's recipe as a gate-only twin),
# B = c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace-ring. First of two A runs run.
# c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace-ring is the control plus EXACTLY two deltas, the engine fabric FABRIC_1D_RING and QWEN_FAST_CCL_TOPOLOGY=ring (test_tp4_next3_cheap_window), so the fabric is the only difference between the arms. Eager J0b measured the ring faster (all-gather 58 against 64 us, reduce-scatter 65 against 84 us per call); its estimate is -2 ms per four-user round. Run E1 (the audited arm) first: if E1 fails, skip these four.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next-3-cheap window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-3-cheap and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image a build-only job builds from this same commit while production serves (it
# carries draft_wide_tp, which is new); a later commit needs a new tag. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3 is a PLACEHOLDER: the driver of the window
# may substitute it (in every template) once the image is built from the pushed branch.
# PRODUCTION IS LIVE ON THE CARDS when the window opens: A0 is the first job and the only one that takes it down.
# The tests: warmup, coding (one stream), concurrent4_code_equal (four real-code prompts of 4k, the padded-4k shape) and
# concurrent4_code_32k (four real-code prompts of 32k, the long-context shape). 800 tokens out each, started together.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 10-20 min on a warm cache (30 min the first time a profile compiles); the four tests
# 15-35 min (the 32k prefill queue dominates): 30-60 min.
# Read: the [PACKED-PHASE] lines (verify: input, trace, sync, readback; commits; early draft; gap) and [PACKED-PUBLISH] medians at 4
# live in each concurrent test: the round wall, the per-user decode_tok_s and the [ACCEPT] mean. Judge the arms PAIRED per round, never
# by unpaired medians; check the load average around the run (a busy host skews host phases 10-20%) and repeat before believing a small
# gap. Then offline: python scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py <A results> <B results> --users 0,1,2,3 --position-keyed
# --strict-concurrent-prefixes (exit 0: every user's text and accepted-prefix sequence identical; 1: a different draft; 2: too few shared
# positions). The served TEXT must be identical between A and B at either exit 0 or 1 (the target verifies every draft); exit 1 is the
# proposals moving, which is acceptance (tau), so read the [ACCEPT] mean beside it. A hang on a timed arm is a finding; both arms carry
# hang fix A (QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_IN_TRACE) and the tail caps, as production does.
# OPTIONAL: the numbers are the product.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent4_code_32k
